This code iterates over the grid and checks if the current character is an oil pocket ('@'). If it is, it checks if it is surrounded by other oil pockets in the 4-connected neighborhood. If not, it increments the count. The algorithm is based on the observation that if an oil deposit is not surrounded by other oil deposits, it must be the source of the deposit. Therefore, we can skip all the '*' characters and only check the '*' characters that are adjacent to '*'. This leads to a time complexity of O(N^2) in the worst case, where N is the number of elements in the grid.

