public static int countOilDeposits(char[][] grid) {
    int count = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < grid[i].length; j++) {
            if (grid[i][j] == '@') {
                count++;
                buildDeposit(i, j, grid);
            }
        }
    }
    return count;
}

private static void buildDeposit(int i, int j, char[][] grid) {
    for (int x = i - 1; x <= i + 1; x++) {
        for (int y = j - 1; y <= j + 1; y++) {
            if (x >= 0 && x < grid.length && y >= 0 && y < grid[x].length) {
                if (grid[x][y] == '@') {
                    grid[x][y] = '*';
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This code first iterates over the grid and for each position that contains an '*' character, it calls the buildDeposit method to build the oil deposit. The buildDeposit method checks the adjacent positions to see if they contain an '*' character, and if so, it replaces the element at that position with a '*' character. This continues until no more '*' characters are found. The number of distinct oil deposits is returned by the countOilDeposits method.

